                <pb facs="0234" n="222" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg222"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultation(2)/279: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Colombia</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Braden</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-07-12T22:00:00-05:00">July 12, 1940—10
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:10 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>189. Department’s circular telegram July 11, 5 p.m. Government project on same
                    topic is very brief but, according to Minister for Foreign Affairs, similar in
                    purpose to Department’s draft and contemplates trusteeship and two-thirds
                    vote.</p>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs leaves for Habana Monday.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Braden</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
